    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0257" n="251" sameAs="frus:frus1901China/pg251"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Rockhill to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 124.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Commissioner of the United States to China</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Peking, China</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1901-06-24"><hi rendition="#italic">June 24,
                                1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: For your further information in connection
                    with my No. 122 of the 22d instant, regarding the military occupation of
                    Shanhaikwan, I inclose herewith translation of a declaration of the Russian
                    military agent in China, reserving to his Government the right of having as
                    Russia’s quota of the garrison at Shanhaikwan as large a number of troops as she
                    may deem necessary to discharge the duties devolving upon her.</p>
                <p>This document should have accompanied my previous dispatch on the subject.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. W. Rockhill.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d150-a1.xml" xpointer="d150-a1"/>
            </div>
